        "mission_intent": "Team, we need to stand up a reporting capability around our supply chain risk management posture, specifically focused on component authenticity controls aligned with NIST 800-53 Rev. 5 SR-11. Please compile a current-state assessment that covers three areas: first, whether we have an active anti-counterfeit training program for relevant personnel and which roles are currently enrolled; second, the status of configuration control procedures for system components that are awaiting service, currently under repair, or queued for return to service, including how we're tracking chain-of-custody through our CMDB and maintenance management workflows; and third, our scanning program for detecting counterfeit components across hardware, software, and firmware inventories. For each area, identify any gaps against the control enhancements and related control families\u2014particularly AT-3, CM-3, MA-2, MA-4, SA-10, and SI-7. Flag where we lack documentation or where procedures exist but aren't being followed. I also need a summary of our external reporting obligations to CISA in the event counterfeit components are discovered. Please have the draft assessment ready for review by end of next week so we can brief leadership the following Monday.",
